  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Going to Georgia** (1 review): Reviewer says audiences usually go wild for this song [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Hello, Old Rabbit**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **Azo Tle Nelli In Tlalticpac?**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Birthday Song: This Time Has Gone**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **Oslo 1888 (Take 1)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Oslo 1888 (Take 2)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Cathedral Song**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **The Window Song**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **The Irony Engine (Franklin Bruno cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: I've Got the Sex, California Song, New Star Song, Nine Black Poppies [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg1996-03-16.aud.128mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 22 songs; 67 min; rated 3/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer finds the audience recording's quality ideal for the era, resembling his own tapes from that time [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- He hasn't begun his storytelling yet; he sometimes dismisses song backstories as a long boring story and moves on [2]\n- Reviewer says the concert resembles his old albums: he wanted to get in and play his songs [2]",
